77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (This magazine is a small beginning, built around a simple belief that meaningful science communication can bring research closer to everyday life. Through stories of remarkable scientists, discoveries that have changed our understanding of the world, and ideas that continue to shape our future, I hope to create a space where curiosity feels welcome, regardless of one's scientific background.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
78 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (Our inaugural cover story features Rosalind Franklin, whose work on X-ray diffraction contributed crucial evidence to the discovery of DNA's structure. Her story invites us to look beyond a scientific breakthrough and consider the people, the work and the history behind it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
