115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Franklin died in 1958, at just 37. By then, the double helix had already become one of the most recognisable structures in science. In the years that followed, her contribution became the subject of considerable debate. Popular retellings often reduced the story to a simple injustice: a brilliant woman produced a photograph, and two men took the discovery from her. The real history is more complicated. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
