/E (It helps in brain mapping and establishing relationships between neural activity and behaviour for understanding neurological disorders such as Parkinsons disease, schizophrenia, depression and epilepsy. It helps researchers go beyond to understand how neural networks work and react to every change in emotion. What once seemed like a far-fetched idea is now a new reality for understanding the organ that makes us who we are.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
