136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (The history of the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine in the new field of optogenetics goes back to the 1970s. In an article in Scientific American, Nobel Laureate Francis Crick famously stated that to study the brain signals, we had to come up with an alternative. The old tools targeted every cell in the brain, and the chemical drugs lacked precision. In 1999, he wrote that the ideal signal would be light but said it was a far-fetched idea at the time. This eventually led to the development of a new field of optogenetics. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
